{"answer":"Exactly 7 subsets have sum 9:\n{1,8}, {2,7}, {3,6}, {4,5}, {1,2,6}, {1,3,5}, and {2,3,4}.\n\nFor example, {1,8} has sum 9. The enumeration below is exhaustive: a subset with four or more positive distinct elements has sum at least 1+2+3+4=10; the possible one-, two-, and three-element cases are then completely listed.","approaches":[{"description":"Classify subsets by cardinality and enumerate the possible ordered elements.","id":"cardinality-enumeration","outcome":"candidate","reason":"It proves both the count and exhaustiveness using only positivity and distinctness."}],"change_log":[],"claims":[{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived by the cardinality bound and exhaustive case enumeration in steps cardinality-bound through total-count.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"total-seven","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"Exactly 7 subsets of {1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8} have sum 9.","step_ids":["cardinality-bound","singleton-case","pair-case","triple-case","total-count"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Explicitly listed in step pair-case.","citations":[],"critical":false,"depends_on":["total-seven"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"example-subset","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"{1,8} is one such subset.","step_ids":["pair-case"],"tool_ids":[]}],"open_questions":[],"proof_steps":[{"citations":[],"depends_on":[],"id":"cardinality-bound","justification":"All elements are distinct positive integers. A subset with at least four elements therefore has sum at least 1+2+3+4=10, so no subset summing to 9 has four or more elements.","statement":"Any subset with sum 9 has at most three elements."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":[],"id":"singleton-case","justification":"No element of the given set equals 9.","statement":"There are no one-element subsets with sum 9."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":[],"id":"pair-case","justification":"Write a pair as {a,b} with a<b and a+b=9. Then a<9/2, so a is one of 1,2,3,4, yielding respectively b=8,7,6,5. These four values all lie in the given set, and no other a is possible.","statement":"The two-element subsets with sum 9 are exactly {1,8}, {2,7}, {3,6}, and {4,5}."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":[],"id":"triple-case","justification":"Write a triple as {a,b,c} with a<b<c and a+b+c=9. If a=1, then b<c and b+c=8, giving b=2,c=6 and b=3,c=5; b=4 would force c=4 and is invalid. If a=2, then b<c and b+c=7, giving b=3,c=4. If a>=3, then a+b+c>=3+4+5=12, impossible. Thus the displayed list is complete.","statement":"The three-element subsets with sum 9 are exactly {1,2,6}, {1,3,5}, and {2,3,4}."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["cardinality-bound","singleton-case","pair-case","triple-case"],"id":"total-count","justification":"By cardinality-bound every relevant subset has one, two, or three elements. The singleton case contributes 0, pair-case contributes 4, and triple-case contributes 3, for 0+4+3=7.","statement":"The enumeration is exhaustive and its total count is 7."}],"question_status":"answered","tool_requests":[]}
